#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:4
msgid "Level of Detail (LOD)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:6
msgid "Level of detail (LOD) is one of the most important ways to optimize rendering (and performance in general) in a 3D project, along with occlusion culling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:10
msgid "The LOD node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:12
msgid "The ``LOD`` node provides a simple way of automatically switching between visual representations as the node gets closer or further from the :ref:`Camera <class_Camera>`, in order to increase performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:16
msgid "You might:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:18
msgid "substitute lower poly count meshes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:19
msgid "swap several separate meshes for a single approximate mesh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:20
msgid "swap from a mesh to a billboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:21
msgid "turn off particle effects, animations, sounds, scripts according to distance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:22
msgid "entirely remove visuals in the distance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:24
msgid "The ``LOD`` node should be added as a parent to whatever you wish to use to show the object, e.g. a :ref:`MeshInstance <class_MeshInstance>`. You can place several :ref:`Spatial <class_Spatial>` derived nodes as children."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:30
msgid "The ``LOD`` node will automatically hide and show Spatial children depending on the distance from the ``Camera``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:35
msgid "You can react to ``NOTIFICATION_VISIBILITY_CHANGED`` in scripts to detect when a node has been shown or hidden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:38
msgid "Children are shown in order with the first children shown when closest to the ``Camera``, and the latter children shown when further away."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:41
msgid "You can determine the distance at which these swaps occur by setting the **lod_range** property of ``Spatial``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:46
msgid "Children of the ``LOD`` node can in turn have any number of children, of any type. These grandchildren will inherit their visibility as the ``LOD`` node operates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:50
msgid "One of the most common cases is to swap between high-poly and low-poly models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:56
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:56
msgid "From most detailed (left) to least detailed (right), wireframe view"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/level_of_detail.rst:60
msgid "Godot 3.x does not currently generate decimated meshes for you. You are advised to generate several versions of a mesh in your modeling program (e.g. using the Decimate modifier in Blender)."
msgstr ""

